WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.188 --> 00:00:02.540
- You pushed the release of your album,

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.530
your new album to honor George Floyd.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.750
How are you interpreting
this moment in our country?

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.460
'Cause you're of the younger generation

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.900
and you're very powerful

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.670
and I think we've all
been really impressed

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.770
with how the younger generation
is handling all of this.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.970
How have you specifically
been handling it?

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.320
- Thank you, yes.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.690
Well, the first couple of weeks,

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:21.850
when everything was happening

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.660
we were definitely just very sad

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.720
and I feel like, collectively,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.610
in our community of our
black brothers and sisters,

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.390
it's like this collective
feeling of just trauma

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.830
when something like that happens

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.290
because for me, personally,

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:38.473
I think of my little
brother, we think of our dad.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.910
That could have been them.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:44.200
So, we just are trying to
do everything that we can

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.560
to continue to lift each
other up with our voices

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.850
and demand justice for what's right.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.010
I mean, our color of our skin

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.390
should not be a death sentence.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:56.356
People deserve to live a
beautiful and long life,

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.190
just like everyone else.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.390
- Exactly, yeah.
- I mean,

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.100
it's crazy that's not a given.

